{
  "_doc": "Parity scenarios run by both twins (python -m coldgas.parity make|check, node tests/parity/make.mjs|check.mjs). init: RigidTwin.reset() init (no task, arm 'start', fixed duration) or task + seed (+ preset) through the task tracker. controller 'random' = mulberry32(seed) valve sequence: per control step and nozzle, a = r(); u = a < p_on ? r() : 0. Checkers replay the golden's u_cmd for 'random', and run the controller itself otherwise. vehicle (optional): partial spec/vehicle.json override passed to both twins (spec/README.md 5.12); the v2-* scenarios cover the touchdown model extensions of 5.11 (per-axle suspension, bump-stop damping / progressive term, slip tyre, wheel spin, floor points, wheel overload incl. the task termination, static toe and compliance steer). drive (optional, spec/README.md 5.13): [[t_start, brake, steer], ...], piecewise-constant drive commands written into action entries NU, NU + 1 from t_start on, on top of whatever the controller returns (also when 'random' replays the golden, which replays drive_cmd too); the drive-* scenarios start rolling on the street (rest-placement equilibrium + speed along the heading, rolling-matched wheel spin) and cover ABS braking, steer steps / reversal / rate limit, brake + steer (also with the slip-ratio saturation wheel_spin.slip_ratio_sat and the sliding blend tyre.slide of 5.11), braking in the air before a touchdown (also with tyre.slide: locked wheels at the touchdown), a kerb hit, thrust + drive (random valves), the v1 override (Coulomb tyre, no spin: brake is a no-op, steer rotates the tyre axes) and the escape-land-stop task (pd + brake overlay, reason 'stopped').",
